🚀 Optimized Single-Pass Solution
The most efficient way to solve this is to keep track of both the largest and secondLargest elements simultaneously in a single pass (O(N) time complexity) without modifying the original array. 
We initialize both trackers to Integer.MIN_VALUE to cleanly handle negative integers. 
java
class Solution {
    public int secondLargestElement(int[] nums) {
        // Edge case: An array must have at least 2 elements to have a second largest
        if (nums == null || nums.length < 2) {
            return -1; 
        }

        int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int secondLargest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num > largest) {
                // The old largest becomes the second largest
                secondLargest = largest;
                largest = num;
            } else if (num > secondLargest && num != largest) {
                // Current number is between largest and second largest
                secondLargest = num;
            }
        }

        // If secondLargest was never updated, a valid second largest doesn't exist (e.g., [10, 10, 10])
        return (secondLargest == Integer.MIN_VALUE) ? -1 : secondLargest;
    }
}



